# Print-in-place fit proof for the whole captive train, as three boolean
# checks on rendered intersections (facet count of the export):
#   fitcheck        empty       — every pairwise intersection of the moving
#                                 bodies (sun/planets/carrier, pairwise and vs
#                                 the housing) renders zero facets: the train
#                                 is free, not fused.
#   fitcheck_neg    interferes  — the planet bore shrunk onto the carrier pin
#                                 (clearance driven 0.6 negative) MUST overlap,
#                                 proving the empty check can fail.
#   fitcheck_phase  interferes  — the sun's mesh phase typo'd from the
#                                 calibrated 15° to 0° MUST collide with the
#                                 planets, proving the phasing constants are
#                                 load-bearing, not decoration (issue #37's
#                                 lesson: a render cannot measure itself).
fitcheck        empty
fitcheck_neg    interferes
fitcheck_phase  interferes
